  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/skeeto/w64devkit/zipball/v2.10.1",
  "body": "* New command: `zip` (Info-ZIP compatible, from [tugz](https://github.com/skeeto/tugz))\r\n  * `gzip`, `gunzip`, `zcat`, and `unzip` replaced with tugz\r\n* New command: `make2compdb` (JSON Compilation Database) [#392]\r\n* GDB Unicode improvements\r\n  * Correct `OutputDebugStringW` display (Windows 10 and later)\r\n  * TUI displays UTF-8 text\r\n* Shell history limit raised to 16k entries, default 1k\r\n* Upgrade to GDB 18.1\r\n* Upgrade to Ccache 4.14.1\r\n* Upgrade to CMake 4.4.4\r\n* Upgrade to NSIS 3.13\r\n* Upgrade to Quilt.cpp 0.69.3\r\n\r\nReleases are self-extracting 7-zip archives, also extractable with any 7z-capable utility (e.g. 7zr.exe). The \"x86\" release is compatible with Windows XP but requires at least a Pentium 4 processor (SSE2).\r\n",
